  <h2>What is Qustodio?</h2>
  <p>
    Qustodio is a commercial parental control and digital wellbeing
    application. Parents install it on their children's devices and supervise
    them from a single dashboard that covers smartphones, tablets, desktops,
    Chromebooks, and more. The company says over 9 million parents use its
    tools. A free plan is available, with paid premium plans for families
    that need more.
  </p>

  <h2>What it offers</h2>
  <p>According to its website, Qustodio's feature set includes:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Web and app filtering — block or allow content and apps.</li>
    <li>Activity monitoring — browsing, social media, and location, in real time.</li>
    <li>Screen-time management — set screen-free times such as study or bedtime.</li>
    <li>Calls and messages monitoring — alerts for concerning messages, with contact blocking.</li>
    <li>Family location — see where devices are, with alerts when they arrive at or leave saved places.</li>
    <li>Daily and weekly activity reports, plus search alerts.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How Guardian Angel is different</h2>
  <p>
    Guardian Angel — our own parental device-management app — covers the
    same ground, but is built around privacy by default:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>No sign-up identity.</strong> No email, no password, no name —
      your account is an anonymous 16-digit number.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Client-side encryption.</strong> Everything the app syncs is
      encrypted on the device with a key only you hold — we cannot read it.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Simple top-up pricing.</strong> $5 / 30 days (Lite) or
      $15 / 30 days (Pro), covering up to 5 devices — prepaid, no
      auto-renewal, and crypto payments save 15%.
    </li>
  </ul>
